WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.270
A colleague ran a pupil's essay

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.630
through an AI detector.

3
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.540
It said ninety-two percent AI.

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.460
The girl cried, because she had

5
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.060
written every word herself.

6
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.180
Today: how AI detectors guess, why

7
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.100
a score is never proof, and fair

8
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.000
rules for AI in your class.

9
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.460
An AI detector can't see who wrote a text.

10
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.790
It looks for patterns that

11
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.170
machine writing often has, like

12
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.390
very even, predictable words.

13
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.460
Then it gives a score: a

14
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.640
guess, not a fact.

15
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.660
Some AI makers add a hidden watermark.

16
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.430
The model quietly prefers certain

17
00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.910
words, its green list, and a

18
00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.770
detector with the key counts them.

19
00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:50.410
Lots of green words means it

20
00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:51.550
was probably the machine.

21
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.960
But a score is never proof.

22
00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.460
Honest writing is sometimes

23
00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.740
flagged by chance.

24
00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.200
Editing two or three words

25
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.760
can erase a watermark.

26
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.520
And studies found that detectors

27
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.640
flag people writing in a second

28
00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:08.920
language more often.

29
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:10.560
Quick check!

30
00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.240
A detector says a pupil's homework

31
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.220
is ninety-two percent AI.

32
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.130
What should happen next?

33
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.300
Talk with the pupil.

34
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.440
Ask them to explain their work, show

35
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.000
their notes or a draft, or write a

36
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.300
short paragraph in class.

37
00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.320
A pupil who wrote it can

38
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.560
usually tell you how.

39
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:33.410
A score alone should never decide a mark.

40
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.600
Better still, set the rules

41
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.320
before anyone is accused.

42
00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.620
Say when AI is allowed, when it

43
00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.280
isn't, and how to show it was used.

44
00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.520
Pupils who know the rules

45
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.100
rarely need a detector.

46
00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:50.730
Put the whole unit together

47
00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.250
as five class rules.

48
00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:54.710
Keep it out: no secrets.

49
00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:56.920
Check it: by the stakes.

50
00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.880
Verify it: on a second channel.

51
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.570
Be fair: nobody is accused on a score.

52
00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.780
And tell someone when

53
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:06.680
something goes wrong.

54
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.180
In my class the rules are on the

55
00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.140
wall, in the pupils' own words.

56
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.320
When something goes wrong, they know they

57
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.220
can tell me without getting into trouble.

58
00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:21.030
In the app, write with the watermark and

59
00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.230
watch the detector count the green words.

60
00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.220
Then write naturally a few times: now and

61
00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.860
then, an honest sentence gets flagged.

62
00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.610
Finally, edit a few words and

63
00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.870
watch the signal fade.

64
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:35.690
Your turn.

65
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.260
Which of these is a fair

66
00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.600
class rule about AI?

67
00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.800
Say when you used AI, and be ready to

68
00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.560
explain: that's clear and fair.

69
00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.260
Remember: a detector's score is a guess,

70
00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.900
and honest writing gets flagged.

71
00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:55.870
Talk before you judge, and agree

72
00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.450
five rules with your class.

73
00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.710
Try it in class tomorrow: write

74
00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:02.930
your five AI rules together.

75
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.980
Take each rule in turn and let

76
00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.040
pupils put it in their own words.

77
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.370
Then put the rules on the wall,

78
00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:11.770
where everyone can see them.
